--TEST--
A `Core` enum that moved into its class has no namespace name left: `Core\Order` names nothing, and the error is reported where it is written — `rule:enums/an-enum-lives-in-the-class-that-uses-it`
--FILE--
<?nvs
array<int> $nums = [3, 1, 2];
echo Core\Arr::sort($nums, {order: Core\Order::Desc})[0], "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `Core\Order` has no constant named `Desc`
  --> case.nvs:3:36
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
